'' THE C++ SPELLINGS, linux-x86_64 -- each name is what clang++ 23 (and g++ 11 on Linux) gives the C++
'' declaration written beside it in src/cxx-names.bas; build/cpplane.sh links the same rules
'' against real C++ objects (docs/tiko-cpp FEASIBILITY 2.3, symbols/manglecxx.ti).
''
''   c1, c2, c3   'byte alias "char"' is plain char, c -- and a repeated 'const char*' is S1_,
''                looked up whole before its parts (it came out PKcPS0_)
''   i1, l1       LP64: 'integer' is C++'s long, l/m (ptrdiff_t, size_t); 'long alias "long"' stays int, i -- C++'s long is 64 bits here
''   v1           '...' is z (it was the v of a parameter with no type)
''   n1           a type nested in a C++ type keeps its case (it was INNER)
''   _Zpl         an operator declared in 'extern "c"': g++ writes the operator alone, as fbc
''                does; clang++ writes _ZplRK1VS1_ -- the compilers disagree (FEASIBILITY 2.3)
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -target linux-x86_64 --dump-mangle tests/mangle/src/cxx-names.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-OUT: _ZN2nm2c1Ec
'' EXPECT-OUT: _ZN2nm2c2Ech
'' EXPECT-OUT: _ZN2nm2c3EPKcS1_
'' EXPECT-OUT: _ZN2nm2i1Elm
'' EXPECT-OUT: _ZN2nm2i2Exy
'' EXPECT-OUT: _ZN2nm2l1Ei
'' EXPECT-OUT: _ZN2nm2v1Eiz
'' EXPECT-OUT: _ZN2nm2n1ENS_5Outer5InnerE
'' EXPECT-OUT: _Zpl
